; NMPC-level (not WBC-level) soft box constraint on the 4 HAA joint angles -
; see createHaaPositionLimitConstraint() in megadog_legged_interface and its
; construction site in MegadogWbcRuntime.cpp. Added after three WBC-level
; mechanisms all failed to narrow HAA past 0.40 rad (see
; MegadogController.cpp's kStandingJointTargetRad comment): real HAA_meas
; was found to track HAA_mpc (the NMPC's own solution) almost exactly, so a
; WBC-level fix - evaluated one control tick after the NMPC already
; committed to a trajectory - could not out-rank it. This constraint is
; instead added directly into the SQP's own OptimalControlProblem,
; evaluated at every transcription node across the whole horizon, so it can
; bend the trajectory before an overshoot instead of reacting to one. Uses
; a SquaredHingePenalty: exactly zero cost until a HAA state gets within
; `delta` rad of `bound`, so it doesn't compete with base/foot tracking
; anywhere except right at the safety edge. bound<=0 disables this
; constraint entirely.
;
; Tested (attempt 4, HAA nominal deliberately left at 0.40 to isolate the
; mechanism) at bound=0.48: peaked 0.482-0.491 rad, right at its own bound
; - this confirmed the natural swing excursion is already this large even
; without any narrowing, closing the question of whether nominal should be
; raised further (it was not, and should not be - see
; kStandingJointTargetRad's comment for the final decision). Kept
; permanently at bound=0.48 as a harmless NMPC-level safety net.
haaPositionLimit
{
  bound   0.48
  mu      80.0
  delta   0.02
}

swingLegTask
{
    kp                   350
    kd                   37
}

weight
{
    swingLeg        100
    baseAccel       1
    contactForce    0.01
}

